# Resource-owner cutover

- `legacy-resource-import.ts`, `account-feature-lifetime.ts` — PR #531 / issue #480: finish authoritative legacy-settlement and terminal/purge resolution; fence and drain old admissions/namespace dispatch before import; checkpoint ownership before activation. Preserve raw evidence, expose unresolved recovery, and never make network resolution an account-boot gate.
- `resource-content-access.ts`, `document-session-registry-implementation.ts`, `local-untitled-owner.ts` — PR #531 / issue #270: hand the exact detached session to authorized transport without replacing its Y.Doc. Preserve persistence and mounted-view identity through remint; make remint and terminal transitions share the namespace lock and drain every account participant.
- `account-feature-lifetime.ts`, resource callers, old lineage/reconciler and `context-catalog-acquisition.ts` — PR #531 / issue #270: compose one account resource owner with the sole reconciliation schedule and catalog installation, cut over every caller, then delete displaced writers and the pending-tree union. Do not production-construct the inactive adapters before that complete cutover.
- `indexeddb-resource-metadata.ts` — verify actual storage exhaustion and storage denial before activation. Chromium quota override did not enforce exhaustion; injected native `QuotaExceededError` rollback passes but does not establish browser eviction behavior.
